- Appium NovaWindows Driver is an independently maintained solution that uses a PowerShell-based backend for Windows UI automation.
- Appium WinCore Driver is officially maintained by the Appium project and uses a .NET-based implementation with Windows UI Automation.

My suggestion would be to proceed with the following approach:

1. Short term: Try using the existing Appium NovaWindows Driver to evaluate its compatibility with our desktop application.
2. In parallel: We could explore downloading and getting approval to install Appium WinCore Driver, allowing us to evaluate it as an alternative solution.

This would enable us to make progress with the tools already available while assessing a more recently developed, officially maintained option.

